# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the dliio concurrency harness
# (test_node_concurrency).
#
# These are NOT data-race bugs. Each access below is serialized by rclcpp
# callback-group mutual exclusion, which establishes a happens-before edge
# through the executor that ThreadSanitizer cannot observe (rclcpp/rmw are not
# TSan-instrumented, so consecutive invocations migrated across executor threads
# look unsynchronized to TSan). Verified by inspection: every member touched
# here is accessed from exactly ONE MutuallyExclusive callback group.
#
# Genuine cross-group races found by this harness WERE fixed (not suppressed):
#   - publishPose reading this->state / imu_stamp  -> now snapshotted under geo.mtx
#   - debug() reading this->state                  -> now snapshotted under geo.mtx
#   - imu_rates write vs publishDiagnostics read   -> guarded by mtx_imu
#   - IMU-buffer iteration vs push_front           -> range copied under mtx_imu
#   - geo.first_opt_done cross-group bool          -> std::atomic<bool>
#   - keyframe_normals/visual_refs concat vs push  -> copied under keyframes_mutex
#
# imu_cb_group (MutuallyExclusive): callbackImu + its helpers own these scalars
# (prev_imu_stamp, first_imu_stamp, imu_meas, calibration accumulators) and the
# transformImu() function-statics; they are never touched off the IMU callback.
race:dlio::OdomNode::transformImu
race:dlio::OdomNode::callbackImu
race:dlio::OdomNode::propagateState
# Pose timer (default MutuallyExclusive group): odom_ros/pose_ros message members
# across serialized timer ticks, plus one constructor->first-tick ordering.
race:dlio::OdomNode::publishPose

# Third-party library noise (not dliio code):
# OpenNI2 (pulled in transitively by PCL's I/O component) unlocks a global mutex
# it did not lock during library load/teardown.
called_from_lib:libOpenNI2
mutex:libOpenNI2
